 uncommitted and must be preserved. Read attached TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rev3.md and TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rev3-addendum.md plus TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev3.md. The predecessor addressed rev3 review; no new immutable CR was visible at the recovery decision. Do not review or accept old CR3.\\n\\nVerify the current candidate and prior validation evidence are present. Reuse applicable completed validation, do not rerun the whole implementation or mutation battery merely to exit. If a check is missing or evidence is invalid, repair that exact gap. Write a task-scoped recovery outcome stating what you verified and what was reused, then perform the required producer handoff and END your final response promptly so the runtime can publish the immutable Change Request. Do not linger after successful handoff. Let managed runtime run required construction checks.\\n\\nNo direct .task-board edits; no cleaning/resetting/staging/committing foreign work. No hand-synthesized commits. No independent product scope or tooling development. CI is local only. No hosted CI activation. Reviewer will be a separate Codex gpt-6-astra medium run after the new CR exists. Full scope remains pinned AX v0.6.0 and actual lease-record identity, union/head derivation, required summary facts, truthful mutation evidence.\\n=====REVIEWER-AFTER=====\\nIndependently review the immutable ready CR produced by RUN-260909-b4446d for TASK-260830-21gygk. Read attached review-verdict-rev3.md and review-evidence-rev3.tar.gz, the rework-rev3.md brief, and results-rev3.md plus results-rev3-addendum.md and the newly delivered validation/mutation resources. The outcome calls this rev3 rework; use the actual new CR identity and tree, never the previously rejected CR3. Preserve the complete assigned v0.6.0 scope and actual task acceptance criteria.\\n\\nCheck closure of all three prior P1 findings through supported production entry points: actual canonical Lease Record identity with same-record facts (including new sessrepo attestation ownership and any changed provhost admission bound); complete lease union/greatest tuple semantics, all required authority heads and parked/unknown sources; required summary observations and exact canonical schema/bounds. Real lease identity, different-attestation refusal, valid lagging copies, and unknown required observations need behavioral evidence, not only renamed tests. Review newly introduced predecessor linkage against the normative contract rather than assuming it is correct. Do not reopen settled predecessor findings unless new changes affect them.\\n\\nEvidence concerns to resolve independently: outcome reports 6/6 AC rows while prior review enumerated 8; derive the denominator from authoritative requirements and map every row. It claims 40N+3B ALL KILLED and says two SURVIVED extras were removed. Verify whether a durable same-instrument successful SURVIVED control is actually delivered, and distinguish green before/after controls from instrument classification capability. Re-derive final counts and inspect exact mutant sources/digests and actual logs. The changed-nonempty record probe still parks due to chain linkage, so it does not exercise a live changed record. Producer claims index/union subsumption: prove that precise claim with a valid witness or source-backed reachability analysis and distinguish a test coverage gap from a demonstrated authorization defect. Do not count refusal-reason ordering as full semantic evidence.\\n\\nProducer reports ENOSPC and deletion of extracted review scratch and /tmp mutant runs. Use attached preserved resources and current exact-candidate evidence; establish missing evidence explicitly. Reuse valid complete evidence where appropriate, with targeted probes for unresolved claims. Avoid needless full suite repetition or giant scratch copies. Do not modify live product files, hand-commit, land, or waive requirements. Use actual merged reviewer checklist and verdict/handoff; accept only when full assigned scope is established, otherwise request precise changes and route back to-dev. Local CI only. Runtime command is /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Reviewer model: codex/gpt-6-astra medium.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5005,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1252,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
