{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca71","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a088c6-4dd5-7de3-9b1f-066ae355783a"},"sequence":915,"recorded_at":1780531400001825,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8693995b-bb36-49e2-b7e2-ad2e4fcb0749","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8693995b-bb36-49e2-b7e2-ad2e4fcb0749","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8693995b-bb36-49e2-b7e2-ad2e4fcb0749"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a088c9-00a5-7342-833e-4577e20b6600"},"task_id":"01a088c9-00a5-7342-833e-4577e20b6600","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a088c9-00a5-7342-833e-4577e20b6600","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-36-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"handoff\\\" ~/.agents/skills/project-management/references/tracked-background-spawn.md 2>&1 | head -n 30; echo \\\"===\\\"; grep -n \\\"outcome\\\" ~/.agents/skills/project-management/references/tracked-background-spawn.md 2>&1 | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Check handoff guidance\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"44:handoff evidence, acceptance, and audit; provider mechanics remain private to\\n392:log and in a board note: `handoff_unsatisfied`, with the detail — the board is\\n572:handoff: acceptance and the `integrating` write are one atomic mutation, so\\n1142:Do not run `task-board handoff` after `worktree integrate`: the transaction\\n1146:remains idempotent; handoff is refused even when its end status is identical.\\n1638:1. A producer's `to-review` handoff triggers an explicitly selected reviewer child immediately.\\n1645:5. A child that exits before handoff or leaves the item parked in `analysis`, `development`, `testing`, or `reviewing` is inspected, retried, or rerouted through a focused child; recoverable work is never handed to the human.\\n1841:appends terminal checklist/outcome handoff evidence without replaying earlier\\n1843:for follow mode, and `wait` only for a barrier that does not need event/handoff\\n1878:`role_handoff` or `reviewer_verdict` owners without replacing the parent\\n1918:Provider usage/budget limits, transient launch or transport failures, nonzero goal-owner exits, unmet producer handoff status/evidence, missing reviewer branches, and unmet delivery acceptance persist a structured recovery cause and automatically queue a successor. A goal-bound predecessor rebinds the same active goal revision; a context-only predecessor drops its predecessor-owned writable child and managed envelope; a run owned by no plane gets an ordinary prompt-mode successor. The predecessor is superseded by recovery, never successful delivery.\\n1977:Producer provider exit is not handoff success. A `role_handoff` run must reach its immutable role end status and add or update a task-scoped outcome artifact relative to its launch snapshot. Zero exit while the board remains in `analysis`/`development`, or at the handoff status without evidence, queues autonomous same-revision recovery.\\n1980:`task-board handoff TASK-ID --role ROLE`. The command resolves the configured\\n2180:  handoff wording, reviewer verdict branches, compact Stop-The-Line evidence\\n2394:**Cause:** Agent ran the first lifecycle commands, then exited before completing the actual work or reaching its role handoff status. Board state looks active even though execution stopped.\\n2396:**Fix:** Always cross-check: `task-board q 'agents()'` + `task-board spawn status RUN-...` + run events/log file modification times. If the process is dead but the task did not reach its producer handoff or reviewer verdict status, inspect run events and outcome resources, then retry or reroute with a focused child run. Use `blocked` only when the evidence proves an external blocker or unresolved human-only stop-the-line decision, and attach the full evidence packet plus the exact human decision or external input needed to resume. Never hand recoverable work to the human or leave a parked intermediate status as the final state.\\n2425:   - After producing handoff evidence: task-board handoff TASK-260212-XXXXXX --role developer\\n2430:   - After producing handoff evidence: task-board handoff TASK-260212-YYYYYY --role developer\\n2527:- Agent reached review handoff successfully.\\n===\\n58:The parent agent is the active Orchestrator role (`orchestrator` / legacy `coordinator`). It creates or selects board tasks, spawns child runs, watches their progress, sends directives when needed, and reads child outcome resources for routing. It should not turn into the worker or reviewer just because a task is small.\\n387:task-scoped outcome artifact. A run that attached nothing is reverted to its\\n393:not at the end status, or no task-scoped outcome artifact was attached.\\n407:that nothing changed and lists the outcome resources that were produced. Deciding\\n513:destroys work existing nowhere else. Both outcomes are reported on the element and\\n553:The `evidence` must also be **this run's own**: a task-scoped outcome resource\\n810:**Three non-passing outcomes, kept apart on purpose.** Collapsing them would\\n876:changes no outcome. There is likewise **no lane attestation and no per-lane\\n1088:The boundary that matters is that **two of the three outcomes cannot be obtained\\n1128:| `change_request_evidence_missing` | the named acceptance evidence is not a task-scoped outcome resource, or is not one this reviewer run attached or updated |\\n1371:| `worktree_trunk_ambiguous` | Compatibility-only `ResolveTrunk` advisory discovery found no unique candidate (or a no-remote checkout had detached `HEAD`); it is not a protected-authority provisioning outcome. |\\n1438:   required test, validation, outcome, and review gates; bounded, mechanical,\\n1562:producer role and one reviewer role, and it must leave an outcome resource with\\n1581:When the smoke fails, save the fresh-session log and board state as an outcome\\n1730:Under `on_deadline: park` that is the deliberate outcome; under\\n1817:Each call returns a `RUN-...` identifier plus a task- and run-scoped logwork path. Concurrent runs for the same task and role therefore keep separate log files and outcome resources. The runner enforces shared concurrency from `task-board.config.json -> spawn.max_parallel` (default `20`), so you can queue more runs than the machine is allowed to execute at once.\\n1841:appends terminal checklist/outcome handoff evidence without replaying earlier\\n1977:Producer provider exit is not handoff success. A `role_handoff` run must reach its immutable role end status and add or update a task-scoped outcome artifact relative to its launch snapshot. Zero exit while the board remains in `analysis`/`development`, or at the handoff status without evidence, queues autonomous same-revision recovery.\\n1979:After attaching the task-scoped outcome, producers should use\\n1982:outcome, then performs the evidence decision and ordinary status transition\\n1983:under one mutation lock. It reports all missing checklist/outcome evidence and\\n1985:producer outcomes, and the runtime still enforces its launch-relative outcome\\n1992:Delivery success is not provider completion alone. Reviewer goals persist exactly one evidence-backed branch derived from board state: `accepted`, `changes_requested`, or `stop_the_line`; an exit while still `reviewing` triggers recovery. `required`/`light` leaves need board `done`, task-scoped producer outcome evidence, and a later reviewer whose persisted branch is `accepted`. `none` leaves need `done`, producer outcome evidence, and the owner’s completion-time evidence check.\\n2102:4. On each wake-up, inspect `spawn status RUN-...` / outcome resources and route the next step (reviewer spawn, rework, dependent task) — then return to waiting on the remaining runs.\\n2179:  metadata/preconditions, task-scoped outcome command, literal `to-review`\\n2195:- Explicit instructions to save results via `task-board m 'add_resource(..., type=outcome)'` on first write and `update_resource(...)` for revisions\\n2198:- Completion-hook contract: if a spawned task lands in `to-review` without a new task-scoped outcome artifact, the hook leaves a blocking note and reverts the task to its start status\\n2240:# (agent runs: task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=TASK-260218-abc_results.md, type=outcome, content=\\\"...\\\", description=\\\"Implementation notes\\\")')\\n2388:4. **Use tracked Claude spawn for research** — reroute through `task-board spawn TASK-260218-abc --agent claude --model claude-opus-5 --role researcher --background` so the child still has a tracked `RUN-...` handle, role lifecycle, and outcome-resource contract while using Claude's larger context\\n2396:**Fix:** Always cross-check: `task-board q 'agents()'` + `task-board spawn status RUN-...` + run events/log file modification times. If the process is dead but the task did not reach its producer handoff or reviewer verdict status, inspect run events and outcome resources, then retry or reroute with a focused child run. Use `blocked` only when the evidence proves an external blocker or unresolved human-only stop-the-line decision, and attach the full evidence packet plus the exact human decision or external input needed to resume. Never hand recoverable work to the human or leave a parked intermediate status as the final state.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8164,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2041,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
